In <news:1161290254.889136.155850@f16g2000cwb.googlegroups.com>,
"defklown" <defklown1000@yahoo.com> wrote:

> Are the following two statements true? Attacking a peaceful creature,
> regardless of chaotic/neutral/lawful, results in a decrease in
> alignment. Killing a previously peaceful creature, regardless of
> chaotic/neutral/lawful, results in a great decrease in alignment.
> 

The first statement is true; the second is not.  The game does not keep
track of "previously peaceful", so after a peaceful monster is angered by
the first attack, it is no longer peaceful and will not have any other
penalties from being "previously peaceful".  However, if you are strong
enough to kill a peaceful creature in one blow, then that gives a -5
alignment penalty, rather than (possibly in addition to) the -1 for
angering a peaceful creature.  Note that unless you're doing a lot of
stuff frequently that lowers alignment, the occasional -1 or even -5 isn't
going to be a big penalty.

> If so, does that mean that if I want to kill, say, a watch captain,
> there's no way to do so without lowering my alignment?
> 

You would always have at least the -1 alignment penalty for angering a
peaceful, but Watch Captains are strong enough you (probably) won't kill
them in a single hit, so you don't need to worry as much about the -5. 
But having a powerful pet is generally considered a better way to get rid
of peaceful creatures you don't want - but be careful, powerful pets can
and will also attack peaceful creatures that you DO want to keep alive -
say, a co-aligned minetown priest.

The appendix of the Praying spoiler includes most of the actions that will
affect your alignment: <http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/pray.html#app>

> Also, does anyone know _exactly_ how sacrificing for artifacts works?
> As in, does anyone know how to calculate the chance of getting an
> artifact, based on your luck, your god's anger, your alignment, the
> difficulty of the monster whose corpse is being sacrificed, or whatever
> else may affect it? If not, is anyone at least certain of which factors
> determine whether or not your god grants you an artifact? Thanks in
> advance.

From <http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/343/art1-343.txt>:
<Table of artifacts, some marked with 'o' in the GENERation column>
 o  This item may be given (non-cursed, and erodeproof if applicable) as
    a gift from your god when #offering corpses.  You must sacrifice a
    fresh corpse at a co-aligned altar, be in good standing with your god,
    have non-negative luck, and be at least experience level 3. You will
    only get artifacts that are of your alignment or none, and some
    classes get certain artifacts as their first gift (if available).
    Your first gift will always be co-aligned.
    Orcs will never receive elven weapons, or vice versa.
    The chance that you will be given a gift depends on the number of
    artifacts already created in the game and how many of them were
    gifts; the chance is 1/(10+(2*artifacts*gifts)).
    If you receive a weapon artifact this way and were restricted in
    its weapon class to unskilled, the restriction is removed so you
    may advance to basic skill.



